{"description": "\"*It*\" is a 1986 horror novel by American author Stephen King. \"*It*\" was his 22nd book and his 17th novel written under his own name. The story follows the experiences of seven children as they are terrorized by an evil entity that exploits the fears of its victims to disguise itself while hunting its prey. \"*It*\" primarily appears in the form of Pennywise the Dancing Clown to attract its preferred prey of young children.\r\n\r\nThe novel won the British Fantasy Award in 1987, and received nominations for the Locus and World Fantasy Awards that same year.\r\n\r\nIn 2003, \"*It*\" was listed at number 144 on the BBC's The Big Read poll.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n----------\r\nSee also:\r\n\r\n - [IT 1/2][2]\r\n - [IT 2/2][3]\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://www.stephenking.com/library/novel/it.html\r\n  [2]: https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14916816W/It_1_2\r\n  [3]: https://openlibrary.org/works/OL14916818W/It_2_2", "links": [{"title": "StephenKing.com - IT", "url": "https://www.stephenking.com/library/novel/it.html", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "It (novel) - Wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/It_(novel)", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "IT | Stephen King Wiki | FANDOM powered by Wikia", "url": "https://stephenking.fandom.com/wiki/IT", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "10 Things You Might Not Know About Stephen King's It | Mental Floss", "url": "http://mentalfloss.com/article/504275/10-things-you-might-not-know-about-stephen-kings-it", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "Reading Stephen King's It is an exhausting way to spend a summer ...", "url": "https://www.theverge.com/2017/9/1/16028300/stephen-king-it-movie-adaptation-book-recap-horror-summer", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "New York Times review", "url": "http://www.nytimes.com/1986/08/21/books/books-of-the-times-547486.html", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}], "title": "It", "covers": [8569284, 9320974, 291381, 8185010, 9156522, 925596